SWAT CLOUD UNIFI AUTO-ADOPT TOOL
=================================

WHAT THIS DOES
--------------
A tech double-clicks "Run-Scan.bat". It:
  1. Detects whatever local network the laptop is currently on (works on
     any site, any IP range - no editing needed).
  2. Scans that network for factory-default UniFi devices (anything with
     SSH open).
  3. Logs into each one with default UniFi credentials and runs
     set-inform http://swatcloud.swatunifi.com:8080/inform
     automatically, twice, for reliability.
  4. Prints a log on screen and saves it to a text file in this folder.

Devices should then appear as "Pending Adoption" in the Swat Cloud
console within a minute or two, ready to be adopted as normal.


ONE-TIME SETUP (do this once, then zip the whole folder and hand it out)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
This folder needs two small free tools added to it before it's ready.
They are NOT included here because they're third-party binaries you
should grab directly from their official sources:

1. NMAP (network scanner)
   - Download the "Nmap for Windows" zip from https://nmap.org/download.html
   - Extract it, find "nmap.exe", copy it into THIS folder
     (the same folder as Run-Scan.bat).
   - Note: this tool only needs nmap's basic TCP connect scan, so the
     separate Npcap driver installer that the full Nmap installer offers
     is NOT required - just the .exe.

2. PLINK (command-line SSH client from the PuTTY suite)
   - Download "plink.exe" directly from
     https://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/putty/latest.html
   - Copy plink.exe into THIS folder too.

Once both .exe files sit next to Scan-And-Adopt.ps1 and Run-Scan.bat,
zip the whole folder. That zip is what you hand to techs - nothing
else needs installing on their laptop, no admin rights needed, works
on Windows Home or Pro.


DEPLOYING TO TECHS
-------------------
- Unzip the folder in a directory with read and write permissions(Desktop is fine).
Install VCredist 64 and 86 both.
- Tech connects the laptop to the site's network (wired or WiFi).
- Tech double-clicks Run-Scan.bat.
- A window opens, shows progress, and pauses at the end so they can
  read the result before closing it.


TROUBLESHOOTING
----------------
- "No devices found": device may not be in factory-default state, may
  already be adopted, or isn't on the same network segment as the
  laptop (e.g. it's on a separate VLAN/switch the laptop can't reach).
- "Could not log into X with default credentials": the device likely
  already has custom SSH credentials, meaning it's probably already
  adopted somewhere or was previously configured.
- If Windows blocks Run-Scan.bat as an unrecognized app (SmartScreen),
  right-click Run-Scan.bat -> Properties -> tick "Unblock" -> OK. This
  is expected the first time on a new laptop and is a one-off per PC.
- The script needs no admin rights and makes no permanent changes to
  the laptop it runs on.


UPDATING THE INFORM URL LATER
-------------------------------
If the cloud controller address ever changes, open Scan-And-Adopt.ps1
in Notepad and edit this single line near the top:
    $informUrl = "http://swatcloud.swatunifi.com:8080/inform"
Save, re-zip, redistribute.
